# Horses and Hineys

2026-10-03

Today, as I sat with my wife as she hunted for a bull moose, one arrived. We heard and spotted a young bull moose - probably around 2 years old. We sat away just 15 meters. He eyeballed us and we eyeballed him. He was beautiful and extremely massive. We hunt for food and not antlers, but given as how his were no bigger than a 3x3 mule deer we knew he was pretty young. He finally got tired of trying to stare us down and ran off, tearing through the grass and woods. Moose know they're the biggest, baddest beasts on the block and he didn't care how much noise he made before or after the encounter.

My sister in law  got a calf elk. It was around a 3 hour ride round trip (and my hiney hurts!) and about 3 hours of sitting on the mountain next to my wife, and then meeting that moose ... what a great and beautiful day. 

We're headed home tomorrow for the workweek and then another 4 days out here. 

Deus vult. 